-- allium: 3
-- keys.allium — SSH keys, deploy keys, SSH principals, GPG keys, signature verification and instance signing.
--
-- Scope: the asymmetric keys people register with the forge and what the
-- forge concludes from them: which SSH key (or certificate principal) a git
-- client authenticated with, whether a commit or tag signature is verified and
-- trusted, and whether the forge itself signs the commits it makes on
-- somebody's behalf.
--
-- Includes:
--   - SshKey: personal SSH public keys (kind personal), the shared key material of
--     deploy keys (kind deploy) and SSH certificate principals (kind principal)
--   - DeployKey: a key attached to one repository with read-only or read-write
--     access; the same key material may be attached to several repositories
--   - Fingerprint uniqueness, allowed algorithms and minimum key sizes
--   - Proving possession of an SSH or GPG key by signing a short-lived token
--     (VerificationChallenge)
--   - SSH keys supplied by an external authentication source (LDAP attribute,
--     OAuth2 provider) and their synchronisation; such keys are read-only to
--     their owner
--   - GpgKey (primary keys and subkeys), GpgKeyImport (the armored original,
--     used for export), the email rule for adding unverified GPG keys
--   - CommitVerification: verifying OpenPGP and SSH signatures on commits and
--     tags, and the per-repository trust model (collaborator / committer /
--     collaborator+committer) that turns a valid signature into
--     trusted / untrusted / unmatched
--   - SigningPolicy and SigningDecision: whether commits the forge creates
--     (initial commit, web edits, merges, wiki edits) are signed with the
--     instance key
--   - What a user exposes publicly: `/{user}.keys`, `/{user}.gpg`, the public
--     key list APIs, and the instance signing keys
--   - Key lookup for SSH authentication (public key or certificate ->
--     registered key) and last-use tracking
--
-- Excludes:
--   - Whether an authenticated SSH key may read or write a given repository,
--     2FA enforcement on SSH, restricted users, archived/mirror push refusal:
--     owned by code (git transport) and access. This module only resolves the
--     presented key to a registered SshKey / DeployKey (SshKeyAuthenticated).
--   - "Require signed commits" on protected branches and the pre-receive check
--     that enforces it: owned by code; it asks this module for a
--     CommitVerification.
--   - The repository's trust_model setting itself (a repository setting):
--     owned by repositories; this module defines TrustModel and its meaning.
--   - authorized_keys / authorized_principals file maintenance (append, full
--     rewrite, backups, AuthorizedKeysCommand template, the
--     resync_all_sshkeys / resync_all_sshprincipals cron tasks, the doctor
--     check): implementation of "a registered key is accepted by the SSH
--     daemon", not behaviour. The built-in SSH server, host keys, ciphers,
--     KEX/MAC lists, listen ports, per-write timeouts and the ssh-keygen vs
--     native parser choice (SSH_KEYGEN_PATH, SSH_KEY_TEST_PATH) are transport
--     implementation.
--   - Accepting a GPG verification signature over "token\n", "token\n\n" or
--     "token\r\n", and the SSH CR LF retry: workarounds for client tooling,
--     folded into "a signature over the token".
--   - Padding of short GPG key ids to 16 characters and stripping leading
--     zeroes in the verify API: presentation / Gitea API compatibility.
--   - SSH2 ("---- BEGIN SSH2 PUBLIC KEY ----") and PEM/PKIX input formats are
--     accepted and normalised to one OpenSSH line; the conversion itself is an
--     implementation detail of ssh_normalised().
--   - The `X-…` Gitea API shapes (key_type "unknown", read_only flag on user
--     keys): API compatibility only.
--
-- Provides to other modules:
--   SshKey.grants_read_on(repository) / grants_write_on(repository)  -- code: deploy key access
--   CommitVerification (answer to SignatureVerificationRequested)    -- code (require signed
--     commits: every new commit's result = verified), releases (tag badges), pulls
--   SigningDecision (answer to the *SigningRequested triggers)       -- code (web edits,
--     can_sign_as), pulls (merge_signing_satisfied), wiki, repositories (initial commit)
--
-- Emits:
--   SshKeyAdded(key, actor)                         -- a user / admin / external source registered a personal key or principal
--   SshKeyDeleted(owner, fingerprint, actor)        -- a personal key or principal was removed
--   DeployKeyAdded(deploy_key, actor)               -- a key was attached to a repository
--   DeployKeyDeleted(repository, name, actor)       -- a key was detached from a repository
--   GpgKeyAdded(key, actor)                         -- a primary GPG key (with its subkeys) was registered
--   GpgKeyDeleted(owner, key_id, actor)             -- a primary GPG key (with its subkeys) was removed
--   SshKeyAuthenticated(connection, key)            -- code: the git client on `connection` holds `key`
--   SignatureVerified(verification)                 -- internal chain: a signature verified, trust to be assessed
--   (CommitVerification and SigningDecision entities are created for the
--    requesting module to read; they are answers, not events.)
--
-- Reacts to:
--   accounts/UserAccountDeleted(user, kind, purge, delete_contributions)  -- remove the user's keys
--   repositories/RepositoryDeleted(repository, doer)                 -- detach deploy keys
--   authentication/ExternalSshKeysAsserted(user, source, keys)       -- source-managed keys (LDAP login /
--                                                                    -- LDAP sync / OAuth2 login)
--   administration/SshKeyAddedForUserByAdmin(admin, user, key_content, title)   -- admin API adds a key
--   administration/SshKeyRemovedForUserByAdmin(admin, user, key)                -- admin API removes a key
--   administration/AuthorizedKeysRewriteDue(), AuthorizedPrincipalsRewriteDue():
--   documented no-op reactions (AuthorizedKeysRewrite / AuthorizedPrincipalsRewrite)
--   — rebuilding the SSH daemon's key files is implementation (see Excludes).
--   administration/AuthorizedKeysRegenerationRequested: likewise, no domain reaction.
--   Requests from other modules, modelled as external stimuli on the
--   ForgeSubsystem surfaces below:
--     SshClientPresentsPublicKey, SshClientPresentsCertificate, SshKeyUsedForRepository  (code: SSH transport)
--     SignatureVerificationRequested  (code, pulls, releases, webhooks payloads, API)
--     InitialCommitSigningRequested, WebEditSigningRequested, WikiEditSigningRequested,
--     MergeSigningRequested           (repositories, code, wiki, pulls)

use "./accounts.allium" as accounts
use "./authentication.allium" as authentication
use "./repositories.allium" as repositories
use "./pulls.allium" as pulls
use "./administration.allium" as administration
use "./access.allium" as access

------------------------------------------------------------
-- External Entities
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Another part of the forge acting on its own behalf (the SSH transport, the
-- LDAP synchroniser, the merge service, the web editor). Used to give the
-- integration surfaces below a party to face.
external entity ForgeSubsystem {
    name: String
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Enumerations
------------------------------------------------------------

-- What a submitted SSH public key turned out to be.
enum SshKeyParseOutcome { valid | private_key | malformed | multiple_keys | unknown_algorithm }

-- Algorithms a key can use. Certificates are classified by their underlying key.
enum SshKeyAlgorithm { ed25519 | ed25519_sk | ecdsa | ecdsa_sk | rsa | dsa }

enum DeployKeyAccess { read_only | read_write }

enum SignatureFormat { openpgp | ssh }

enum SignedObjectKind { commit | tag }

-- How a repository decides whether a valid signature is trusted.
-- `instance_default` (Forgejo: "default") means "use config.default_trust_model".
enum TrustModel { instance_default | collaborator | committer | collaborator_committer }

enum TrustStatus { trusted | untrusted | unmatched }

enum VerificationResult { verified | unverified | warning }

enum VerificationReason {
    not_signed                -- the object carries no signature
    | unreadable_signature    -- the signature block could not be parsed
    | signed_by_user_key      -- a registered user key produced the signature
    | signed_by_instance_key  -- the forge's own signing key produced the signature
    | probable_bad_signature  -- the signature names a key we know, but that key did not produce it
    | no_matching_key         -- no registered or instance key produced the signature
}

-- The commits the forge creates itself and may sign.
enum SignedOperation { initial_commit | web_edit | merge | wiki_edit }

enum SigningMode { never | always | conditional }

-- One entry of a [repository.signing] list (INITIAL_COMMIT, CRUD_ACTIONS,
-- MERGES, WIKI), as written in app.ini.
enum SigningListEntry {
    never | always | pubkey | twofa | parentsigned
    | basesigned | headsigned | commitssigned | approved
}

-- Why the forge declined to sign (the first failing condition).
enum SigningRefusal {
    no_instance_key        -- no signing key configured / available ("nokey")
    | policy_never         -- policy is "never"
    | no_registered_key    -- "pubkey": the actor has no GPG key or personal SSH key
    | no_two_factor        -- "twofa": the actor has no second factor enrolled
    | parent_unsigned      -- "parentsigned": the parent commit is not verified
    | base_unsigned        -- "basesigned": the merge base head is not verified
    | head_unsigned        -- "headsigned": the PR head commit is not verified
    | commits_unsigned     -- "commitssigned": some PR commit is not verified
    | not_approved         -- "approved": no protected-branch approval on the PR
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Entities and Variants
------------------------------------------------------------

-- A registered SSH public key, or an SSH certificate principal.
--   kind personal  : a personal key of `owner`; authenticates as that user.
--   kind deploy    : key material attached to one or more repositories through
--                    DeployKey; it has no owner and authenticates only for
--                    the repositories it is attached to.
--   kind principal : not a key at all but a principal name; a client presenting
--                    a certificate from a trusted CA naming this principal
--                    authenticates as `owner`.
-- from: models/asymkey/ssh_key.go:38
entity SshKey {
    kind: personal | deploy | principal
    owner: accounts/User?                 -- set for user and principal keys, absent for deploy keys
    name: String                          -- title; for a principal it equals the principal
    content: String                       -- one normalised OpenSSH line ("type base64 comment"), or the principal
    fingerprint: String?                  -- SHA256 fingerprint; absent for principals
    algorithm: SshKeyAlgorithm?           -- absent for principals
    bits: Integer?                        -- absent for principals
    auth_source: authentication/AuthSource?   -- set when the key was supplied by an external source
    is_verified: Boolean                  -- possession proven by signing a token (personal keys only)
    created_at: Timestamp
    last_used_at: Timestamp?              -- last successful SSH use

    -- Relationships
    attachments: DeployKey with key = this

    -- What a deploy key may do in a repository (code asks these when a git
    -- client authenticated with this key).
    grants_read_on(repository): kind = deploy and attachments.any(d => d.repository = repository)
    grants_write_on(repository): kind = deploy and attachments.any(d => d.repository = repository and d.access = read_write)

    -- Derived
    has_been_used: last_used_at != null
    has_recent_activity: last_used_at != null and last_used_at + config.recent_activity_window > now
    -- A key supplied by a source that (still) provides SSH keys is managed there,
    -- not by its owner. If the source has been deleted the key becomes ordinary.
    -- from: models/asymkey/ssh_key.go:267
    is_externally_managed: auth_source != null and auth_source.provides_ssh_keys
    -- The key line without its trailing comment (which often holds an email).
    -- from: models/asymkey/ssh_key.go:66
    public_line: without_comment(content)
}

-- One repository's grant to an SSH key.
-- from: models/asymkey/ssh_key_deploy.go:28
entity DeployKey {
    repository: repositories/Repository
    key: SshKey
    name: String                          -- unique within the repository
    access: DeployKeyAccess
    created_at: Timestamp
    last_used_at: Timestamp?

    is_read_only: access = read_only
    has_recent_activity: last_used_at != null and last_used_at + config.recent_activity_window > now
}

-- A GPG public key. Primary keys have no `primary`; subkeys point at their
-- primary key and share its owner.
-- from: models/asymkey/gpg_key.go:23
entity GpgKey {
    owner: accounts/User
    key_id: String                        -- 16-hex-digit long key id, unique across the instance
    primary: GpgKey?                      -- set for subkeys
    public_key: String                    -- the (sub)key's public key packet
    identity_emails: Set<String>          -- emails of the primary key's non-revoked user ids (empty for subkeys)
    key_created_at: Timestamp             -- creation time recorded in the key
    expires_at: Timestamp?                -- absent when the key never expires
    added_at: Timestamp
    is_verified: Boolean                  -- possession proven by signing a token
    can_sign: Boolean
    can_encrypt_comms: Boolean
    can_encrypt_storage: Boolean
    can_certify: Boolean

    -- Relationships
    subkeys: GpgKey with primary = this
    original_import: GpgKeyImport with key = this

    -- Derived
    is_primary: primary = null
    is_expired: expires_at != null and expires_at <= now
    -- Identity emails that are activated addresses of the owner (case-insensitive).
    -- from: models/asymkey/gpg_key.go:169
    matched_emails: activated_identity_emails(owner, identity_emails)
    -- A key may vouch for signatures when its holder proved possession or one of
    -- its identities is an activated address of the owner.
    -- from: models/asymkey/gpg_key.go:252
    is_usable_for_signatures: is_verified or has_activated_identity(owner, identity_emails)
}

-- The armored block a primary GPG key was uploaded in, kept verbatim so the
-- user's keys can be exported again with their signatures and identities.
-- from: models/asymkey/gpg_key_import.go:24
entity GpgKeyImport {
    key: GpgKey
    armored: String
}

-- A short-lived token a user signs with a key to prove they hold it.
-- from: models/asymkey/gpg_key_verify.go:111
entity VerificationChallenge {
    owner: accounts/User
    token: String
    issued_at: Timestamp
    expires_at: Timestamp
    status: open | expired

    transitions status {
        open -> expired
        terminal: expired
    }
}

-- The answer to "is this commit / tag signature verified, and is it trusted
-- in this repository?". Created on request; never edited by users.
-- from: models/asymkey/gpg_key_object_verification.go:27
entity CommitVerification {
    repository: repositories/Repository
    object_kind: SignedObjectKind
    object_id: String                     -- commit or tag object id
    committer_email: String               -- committer (or tagger) email recorded in the object
    committer: accounts/User?             -- account owning that email (activated, or the user's no-reply address)
    format: SignatureFormat?              -- absent when unsigned
    result: VerificationResult
    reason: VerificationReason
    signer: accounts/User?                -- user whose key produced the signature
    signed_by_instance: Boolean           -- the forge's own key produced the signature
    signing_email: String?                -- email the signer is credited with
    signing_gpg_key: GpgKey?
    signing_ssh_key: SshKey?
    trust: TrustStatus?                   -- set when result = verified

    -- What a reader is shown: green, yellow, orange, red or grey.
    -- from: templates/repo/commit_page.tmpl (badge classes)
    is_trusted: result = verified and trust = trusted
}

-- How one kind of forge-made commit is signed. One instance per operation,
-- materialised from the [repository.signing] lists in config at start-up
-- (INITIAL_COMMIT, CRUD_ACTIONS, MERGES, WIKI). A list containing "never"
-- gives mode never; one containing "always" gives mode always; an empty or
-- unrecognised list gives mode never; otherwise mode conditional with one
-- flag per listed condition. Conditions that do not apply to an operation are
-- ignored (see invariant SigningConditionsApply).
-- from: services/asymkey/sign.go:39
entity SigningPolicy {
    operation: SignedOperation
    mode: SigningMode
    requires_registered_key: Boolean      -- "pubkey"
    requires_two_factor: Boolean          -- "twofa"
    requires_parent_signed: Boolean       -- "parentsigned" (web_edit, wiki_edit)
    requires_base_signed: Boolean         -- "basesigned"   (merge)
    requires_head_signed: Boolean         -- "headsigned"   (merge)
    requires_commits_signed: Boolean      -- "commitssigned" (merge)
    requires_approval: Boolean            -- "approved"     (merge)
}

-- The forge's decision on whether to sign one commit it is about to create.
-- from: services/asymkey/sign.go:139
entity SigningDecision {
    operation: SignedOperation
    actor: accounts/User
    repository: repositories/Repository
    will_sign: Boolean
    refusal: SigningRefusal?              -- set when will_sign = false
    signer_name: String?                  -- identity the commit is signed as, when will_sign
    signer_email: String?
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Config
------------------------------------------------------------

config {
    -- [server]
    ssh_disabled: Boolean = false                       -- DISABLE_SSH
    minimum_key_size_check: Boolean = true              -- MINIMUM_KEY_SIZE_CHECK

    -- [ssh.minimum_key_sizes]: minimum bits per algorithm; -1 forbids the
    -- algorithm entirely. An algorithm without an entry is forbidden (DSA).
    min_bits_ed25519: Integer = 256                     -- ED25519
    min_bits_ed25519_sk: Integer = 256                  -- ED25519-SK
    min_bits_ecdsa: Integer = 256                       -- ECDSA
    min_bits_ecdsa_sk: Integer = 256                    -- ECDSA-SK
    min_bits_rsa: Integer = 3071                        -- RSA
    min_bits_dsa: Integer = -1                          -- DSA (no entry by default: forbidden)

    -- [server] SSH certificates. SSH_TRUSTED_USER_CA_KEYS lists the CAs whose
    -- user certificates are accepted. SSH_AUTHORIZED_PRINCIPALS_ALLOW decides
    -- which principals a user may register: "off", or any of "username",
    -- "email", "anything". Its default is "username,email" when trusted CA keys
    -- are configured and "off" otherwise.
    trusted_user_ca_keys_configured: Boolean = false    -- SSH_TRUSTED_USER_CA_KEYS non-empty
    principals_allow_username: Boolean = false          -- SSH_AUTHORIZED_PRINCIPALS_ALLOW contains username
    principals_allow_email: Boolean = false             -- SSH_AUTHORIZED_PRINCIPALS_ALLOW contains email
    principals_allow_anything: Boolean = false          -- SSH_AUTHORIZED_PRINCIPALS_ALLOW contains anything

    -- [repository.signing]
    signing_key: String = "default"                     -- SIGNING_KEY: "none", "default" (the server's git/gpg config), a GPG key id, or (ssh format) a public key file
    signing_name: String = ""                           -- SIGNING_NAME
    signing_email: String = ""                          -- SIGNING_EMAIL
    signing_format: SignatureFormat = openpgp           -- FORMAT
    initial_commit_signing: Set<SigningListEntry> = {always}           -- INITIAL_COMMIT (materialised as SigningPolicy initial_commit)
    crud_actions_signing: Set<SigningListEntry> = {pubkey, twofa, parentsigned}   -- CRUD_ACTIONS (SigningPolicy web_edit)
    merges_signing: Set<SigningListEntry> = {pubkey, twofa, basesigned, commitssigned}  -- MERGES (SigningPolicy merge)
    wiki_signing: Set<SigningListEntry> = {never}                      -- WIKI (SigningPolicy wiki_edit)
    default_trust_model: TrustModel = collaborator      -- DEFAULT_TRUST_MODEL ("default" also means collaborator; instance_default is not a valid value here)

    -- Hard-coded in Forgejo
    recent_activity_window: Duration = 7.days           -- "used recently" marker on key lists
    verification_token_lifetime: Duration = 2.minutes   -- a token stays signable for the rest of its minute and the next
    title_max_length: Integer = 50                      -- key / deploy key title limit (web form)
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: personal SSH keys
------------------------------------------------------------

-- A user registers one of their SSH public keys.
-- The key must parse as a single public key, use an allowed algorithm with
-- enough bits, and have a fingerprint no other key (personal, deploy or
-- otherwise) already uses. Titles are unique per owner.
-- from: routers/web/user/setting/keys.go:163
rule UserAddsSshKey {
    when: UserAddsSshKey(owner, title, content)

    let fingerprint = ssh_fingerprint(content)
    let algorithm = ssh_key_algorithm(content)
    let bits = ssh_key_bits(content)

    requires: manages_own_ssh_keys(owner)
    requires: title != "" and length(title) <= config.title_max_length
    requires: ssh_parse_outcome(content) = valid
    requires: not config.minimum_key_size_check
        or (algorithm = ed25519 and config.min_bits_ed25519 >= 0 and bits >= config.min_bits_ed25519)
        or (algorithm = ed25519_sk and config.min_bits_ed25519_sk >= 0 and bits >= config.min_bits_ed25519_sk)
        or (algorithm = ecdsa and config.min_bits_ecdsa >= 0 and bits >= config.min_bits_ecdsa)
        or (algorithm = ecdsa_sk and config.min_bits_ecdsa_sk >= 0 and bits >= config.min_bits_ecdsa_sk)
        or (algorithm = rsa and config.min_bits_rsa >= 0 and bits >= config.min_bits_rsa)
        or (algorithm = dsa and config.min_bits_dsa >= 0 and bits >= config.min_bits_dsa)
    requires: not exists SshKey{fingerprint: fingerprint}
    requires: not exists SshKey{owner: owner, name: title}

    ensures:
        let key = SshKey.created(
            kind: personal,
            owner: owner,
            name: title,
            content: ssh_normalised(content),
            fingerprint: fingerprint,
            algorithm: algorithm,
            bits: bits,
            auth_source: null,
            is_verified: false,
            created_at: now,
            last_used_at: null
        )
        SshKeyAdded(key: key, actor: owner)

    @guidance
        -- Web: POST /user/settings/keys (type=ssh). API: POST /api/v1/user/keys.
        -- Input may be OpenSSH, SSH2 or PEM/PKIX; it is normalised to one
        -- OpenSSH line. A private key is refused with a dedicated message
        -- (ssh_parse_outcome = private_key) so the user knows they pasted the
        -- wrong half.
}

-- An administrator registers an SSH key on behalf of a user (API only). The
-- admin surface and permission check live in administration; this rule is
-- the key-side effect with the same validation as a user's own addition.
-- from: routers/api/v1/admin/user.go:329
rule AddSshKeyForUserByAdmin {
    when: administration/SshKeyAddedForUserByAdmin(admin, user, key_content, title)

    let fingerprint = ssh_fingerprint(key_content)
    let algorithm = ssh_key_algorithm(key_content)
    let bits = ssh_key_bits(key_content)

    requires: admin.is_admin
    requires: manages_own_ssh_keys(admin)
    requires: title != ""
    requires: ssh_parse_outcome(key_content) = valid
    requires: not config.minimum_key_size_check
        or (algorithm = ed25519 and config.min_bits_ed25519 >= 0 and bits >= config.min_bits_ed25519)
        or (algorithm = ed25519_sk and config.min_bits_ed25519_sk >= 0 and bits >= config.min_bits_ed25519_sk)
        or (algorithm = ecdsa and config.min_bits_ecdsa >= 0 and bits >= config.min_bits_ecdsa)
        or (algorithm = ecdsa_sk and config.min_bits_ecdsa_sk >= 0 and bits >= config.min_bits_ecdsa_sk)
        or (algorithm = rsa and config.min_bits_rsa >= 0 and bits >= config.min_bits_rsa)
        or (algorithm = dsa and config.min_bits_dsa >= 0 and bits >= config.min_bits_dsa)
    requires: not exists SshKey{fingerprint: fingerprint}
    requires: not exists SshKey{owner: user, name: title}

    ensures:
        let key = SshKey.created(
            kind: personal,
            owner: user,
            name: title,
            content: ssh_normalised(key_content),
            fingerprint: fingerprint,
            algorithm: algorithm,
            bits: bits,
            auth_source: null,
            is_verified: false,
            created_at: now,
            last_used_at: null
        )
        SshKeyAdded(key: key, actor: admin)

    @guidance
        -- API: POST /api/v1/admin/users/{username}/keys.
}

-- A user asks for a token to sign. The same token serves SSH and GPG proofs.
-- from: routers/api/v1/user/gpg_key.go:191
rule UserRequestsVerificationToken {
    when: UserRequestsVerificationToken(owner)

    ensures: VerificationChallenge.created(
        owner: owner,
        token: new_verification_token(owner),
        issued_at: now,
        expires_at: now + config.verification_token_lifetime,
        status: open
    )

    @guidance
        -- Web: shown on /user/settings/keys whenever a verify form is open.
        -- API: GET /api/v1/user/gpg_key_token.
        -- Forgejo derives the token deterministically from the current minute
        -- and the user's identity, so no state is kept; a rebuild may store it.
}

-- from: models/asymkey/gpg_key_verify.go:111
rule VerificationChallengeExpires {
    when: challenge: VerificationChallenge.expires_at <= now
    requires: challenge.status = open
    ensures: challenge.status = expired
}

-- A user proves they hold the private half of one of their SSH keys by
-- signing the token (`ssh-keygen -Y sign -n <instance domain>`).
-- from: models/asymkey/ssh_key_verify.go:17
rule UserVerifiesSshKey {
    when: UserVerifiesSshKey(owner, key, challenge, signature)

    requires: manages_own_ssh_keys(owner)
    requires: key.kind = personal
    requires: key.owner = owner
    requires: challenge.owner = owner
    requires: challenge.status = open
    requires: ssh_signs_token(key, signature, challenge.token)

    ensures: key.is_verified = true

    @guidance
        -- Web: POST /user/settings/keys (type=verify_ssh, fingerprint, signature).
        -- The SSH signature namespace is the instance's domain, so a
        -- signature made for another forge does not verify here.
}

-- A user removes one of their keys; an administrator may remove anyone's.
-- Keys managed by an external source cannot be removed this way.
-- from: services/asymkey/ssh_key.go:17
rule UserDeletesSshKey {
    when: UserDeletesSshKey(actor, key)
    -- read before the record goes: an emission sees the resulting state
    let key_owner = key.owner
    let key_fingerprint = key.fingerprint

    requires: manages_own_ssh_keys(actor)
    requires: key.kind = personal
    requires: key.owner = actor or actor.is_admin
    requires: not key.is_externally_managed

    ensures: not exists key
    ensures: SshKeyDeleted(owner: key_owner, fingerprint: key_fingerprint, actor: actor)

    @guidance
        -- Web: POST /user/settings/keys/delete (type=ssh). API: DELETE /api/v1/user/keys/{id}.
}

-- An administrator removes a key from a given user's account (API). The
-- admin surface lives in administration.
-- from: routers/api/v1/admin/user.go:361
rule RemoveSshKeyOfUserByAdmin {
    when: administration/SshKeyRemovedForUserByAdmin(admin, user, key)
    -- read before the record goes: an emission sees the resulting state
    let key_fingerprint = key.fingerprint

    requires: admin.is_admin
    requires: key.kind in {personal, principal}
    requires: key.owner = user

    ensures: not exists key
    ensures: SshKeyDeleted(owner: user, fingerprint: key_fingerprint, actor: admin)

    @guidance
        -- API: DELETE /api/v1/admin/users/{username}/keys/{id}. Unlike the
        -- user's own deletion this also removes externally managed keys.
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: SSH certificate principals
------------------------------------------------------------

-- A user registers a principal so certificates naming it log them in.
-- from: models/asymkey/ssh_key_principals.go:58
rule UserAddsPrincipal {
    when: UserAddsPrincipal(owner, principal)

    let value = trimmed(principal)

    requires: not config.ssh_disabled
    requires: config.principals_allow_anything or config.principals_allow_username or config.principals_allow_email
    requires: is_single_line(value)
    requires: config.principals_allow_anything
        or (config.principals_allow_username and value = owner.name)
        or (config.principals_allow_email and owner.activated_emails.any(e => e.address = value))
    requires: not exists SshKey{kind: principal, content: value}
    requires: not exists SshKey{owner: owner, name: value}

    ensures:
        let key = SshKey.created(
            kind: principal,
            owner: owner,
            name: value,
            content: value,
            fingerprint: null,
            algorithm: null,
            bits: null,
            auth_source: null,
            is_verified: false,
            created_at: now,
            last_used_at: null
        )
        SshKeyAdded(key: key, actor: owner)

    @guidance
        -- Web only: POST /user/settings/keys (type=principal). The form is
        -- hidden unless principals are enabled.
}

-- from: routers/web/user/setting/keys.go:277
rule UserDeletesPrincipal {
    when: UserDeletesPrincipal(actor, key)
    -- read before the record goes: an emission sees the resulting state
    let key_owner = key.owner

    requires: key.kind = principal
    requires: key.owner = actor or actor.is_admin

    ensures: not exists key
    ensures: SshKeyDeleted(owner: key_owner, fingerprint: null, actor: actor)
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: SSH keys from external authentication sources
------------------------------------------------------------

-- An external source (LDAP attribute on login or sync, OAuth2 provider on
-- login) reports the SSH keys a user should have. Keys new to the user are
-- added, named "<source name>-<fingerprint>" and tied to the source. Keys
-- whose fingerprint is already registered anywhere, or which do not parse,
-- are skipped silently.
-- from: models/asymkey/ssh_key.go:321
rule AddExternallySuppliedSshKeys {
    when: authentication/ExternalSshKeysAsserted(user, source, keys)

    requires: source.provides_ssh_keys

    ensures:
        for content in keys:
            if ssh_parse_outcome(content) = valid and not exists SshKey{fingerprint: ssh_fingerprint(content)}:
                let key = SshKey.created(
                    kind: personal,
                    owner: user,
                    name: source.name + "-" + ssh_fingerprint(content),
                    content: ssh_normalised(content),
                    fingerprint: ssh_fingerprint(content),
                    algorithm: ssh_key_algorithm(content),
                    bits: ssh_key_bits(content),
                    auth_source: source,
                    is_verified: false,
                    created_at: now,
                    last_used_at: null
                )
                SshKeyAdded(key: key, actor: user)

    @guidance
        -- Key size and algorithm policy is NOT applied to externally supplied
        -- keys in Forgejo (see open questions). Keys already registered
        -- (by fingerprint, to anyone) and unparseable entries are skipped.
}

-- Keys previously supplied by this source that it no longer reports are removed.
-- from: models/asymkey/ssh_key.go:359
rule RemoveWithdrawnExternalSshKeys {
    when: authentication/ExternalSshKeysAsserted(user, source, keys)

    let still_published = presented_public_lines(keys)

    requires: source.provides_ssh_keys

    ensures:
        for key in SshKeys where owner = user and auth_source = source and public_line not in still_published:
            ExternalSshKeyWithdrawn(key: key, user: user)
}

-- One withdrawn key goes. Its fingerprint is read before it does: the
-- deletion event is about a key that no longer exists.
-- from: services/asymkey/ssh_key_authorized_keys.go:142
rule RemoveWithdrawnExternalSshKey {
    when: ExternalSshKeyWithdrawn(key, user)
    let withdrawn_fingerprint = key.fingerprint
    ensures: not exists key
    ensures: SshKeyDeleted(owner: user, fingerprint: withdrawn_fingerprint, actor: user)
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: deploy keys
------------------------------------------------------------

-- A repository administrator grants an SSH key read-only or read-write git
-- access to the repository. The key material may already be a deploy key of
-- other repositories (it is then shared), but never a personal key or
-- principal.
-- from: models/asymkey/ssh_key_deploy.go:109
rule RepoAdminAddsDeployKey {
    when: RepoAdminAddsDeployKey(admin, repository, title, content, access)

    let fingerprint = ssh_fingerprint(content)
    let algorithm = ssh_key_algorithm(content)
    let bits = ssh_key_bits(content)
    let existing = SshKey{fingerprint: fingerprint}

    requires: is_repo_admin(admin, repository)
    requires: title != "" and length(title) <= config.title_max_length
    requires: ssh_parse_outcome(content) = valid
    requires: not config.minimum_key_size_check
        or (algorithm = ed25519 and config.min_bits_ed25519 >= 0 and bits >= config.min_bits_ed25519)
        or (algorithm = ed25519_sk and config.min_bits_ed25519_sk >= 0 and bits >= config.min_bits_ed25519_sk)
        or (algorithm = ecdsa and config.min_bits_ecdsa >= 0 and bits >= config.min_bits_ecdsa)
        or (algorithm = ecdsa_sk and config.min_bits_ecdsa_sk >= 0 and bits >= config.min_bits_ecdsa_sk)
        or (algorithm = rsa and config.min_bits_rsa >= 0 and bits >= config.min_bits_rsa)
        or (algorithm = dsa and config.min_bits_dsa >= 0 and bits >= config.min_bits_dsa)
    requires: not exists existing or existing.kind = deploy
    requires: not exists existing or not exists DeployKey{repository: repository, key: existing}
    requires: not exists DeployKey{repository: repository, name: title}

    ensures:
        if exists existing:
            let attached = DeployKey.created(
                repository: repository,
                key: existing,
                name: title,
                access: access,
                created_at: now,
                last_used_at: null
            )
            DeployKeyAdded(deploy_key: attached, actor: admin)
        else:
            let material = SshKey.created(
                kind: deploy,
                owner: null,
                name: title,
                content: ssh_normalised(content),
                fingerprint: fingerprint,
                algorithm: algorithm,
                bits: bits,
                auth_source: null,
                is_verified: false,
                created_at: now,
                last_used_at: null
            )
            let fresh = DeployKey.created(
                repository: repository,
                key: material,
                name: title,
                access: access,
                created_at: now,
                last_used_at: null
            )
            DeployKeyAdded(deploy_key: fresh, actor: admin)

    @guidance
        -- Web: POST /{owner}/{repo}/settings/keys (is_writable checkbox).
        -- API: POST /api/v1/repos/{owner}/{repo}/keys (read_only flag).
        -- Both require repository admin access (API: a token with repository scope).
}

-- A repository administrator detaches a deploy key. When no repository uses
-- the key material any more, the material is forgotten too.
-- from: models/repo.go:278
rule RepoAdminDeletesDeployKey {
    when: RepoAdminDeletesDeployKey(admin, deploy_key)
    -- read before the record goes: an emission sees the resulting state
    let key_repository = deploy_key.repository
    let key_name = deploy_key.name

    let material = deploy_key.key
    let shared = material.attachments.count > 1

    requires: is_repo_admin(admin, deploy_key.repository)

    ensures: not exists deploy_key
    ensures:
        if not shared:
            not exists material
    ensures: DeployKeyDeleted(repository: key_repository, name: key_name, actor: admin)

    @guidance
        -- Web: POST /{owner}/{repo}/settings/keys/delete.
        -- API: DELETE /api/v1/repos/{owner}/{repo}/keys/{id}; a key id that
        -- belongs to another repository is refused.
}

-- Deleting a repository detaches all its deploy keys (and forgets material
-- no other repository uses).
-- from: services/repository/delete.go:106
rule DetachDeployKeysOfDeletedRepository {
    when: repositories/RepositoryDeleted(repository, doer)

    for deploy_key in DeployKeys where repository = repository:
        let material = deploy_key.key
        let shared = material.attachments.count > 1
        ensures: not exists deploy_key
        ensures:
            if not shared:
                not exists material
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: scheduled key-file rewrites
------------------------------------------------------------

-- administration's resync_all_sshkeys cron task. Rewriting the SSH daemon's
-- authorized_keys file from SshKeys is an implementation detail (see
-- Excludes): the keys themselves do not change, so this reaction is a
-- documented no-op that only marks that the rewrite was asked for.
-- from: services/cron/tasks_extended.go (resync_all_sshkeys)
rule AuthorizedKeysRewrite {
    when: administration/AuthorizedKeysRewriteDue()
    ensures: KeyFileRewriteRequested(kind: authorized_keys)
}

-- administration's resync_all_sshprincipals cron task; as above, for the
-- authorized_principals file.
-- from: services/cron/tasks_extended.go (resync_all_sshprincipals)
rule AuthorizedPrincipalsRewrite {
    when: administration/AuthorizedPrincipalsRewriteDue()
    ensures: KeyFileRewriteRequested(kind: authorized_principals)
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: account deletion
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Deleting an account removes its SSH keys, principals, GPG keys and imports.
-- from: services/user/delete.go:213
rule RemoveKeysOfDeletedAccount {
    when: accounts/UserAccountDeleted(user, kind, purge, delete_contributions)

    ensures:
        for key in SshKeys where owner = user:
            not exists key
    ensures:
        for gpg in GpgKeys where owner = user:
            not exists gpg
    ensures:
        for imported in GpgKeyImports where key.owner = user:
            not exists imported
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: GPG keys
------------------------------------------------------------

-- A user adds a GPG key without proving possession. It is accepted only if one
-- of its (non-revoked) identities is an activated email address of the user.
-- The key is stored unverified.
-- from: models/asymkey/gpg_key_add.go:349
rule UserAddsGpgKeyMatchedByEmail {
    when: UserAddsGpgKey(owner, armored)

    let key_id = gpg_primary_key_id(armored)
    let identities = gpg_identity_emails(armored)

    requires: manages_own_gpg_keys(owner)
    requires: gpg_armored_key_parses(armored)
    requires: not exists GpgKey{key_id: key_id}
    requires: has_activated_identity(owner, identities)

    ensures:
        let key = GpgKey.created(
            owner: owner,
            key_id: key_id,
            primary: null,
            public_key: gpg_primary_public_key(armored),
            identity_emails: identities,
            key_created_at: gpg_key_created_at(armored, key_id),
            expires_at: gpg_key_expires_at(armored, key_id),
            added_at: now,
            is_verified: false,
            can_sign: gpg_key_can_sign(armored, key_id),
            can_encrypt_comms: gpg_key_can_encrypt(armored, key_id),
            can_encrypt_storage: gpg_key_can_encrypt(armored, key_id),
            can_certify: gpg_key_can_certify(armored, key_id)
        )
        GpgKeyImport.created(key: key, armored: armored)
        for sub_id in gpg_subkey_ids(armored):
            GpgKey.created(
                owner: owner,
                key_id: sub_id,
                primary: key,
                public_key: gpg_subkey_public_key(armored, sub_id),
                identity_emails: {},
                key_created_at: gpg_key_created_at(armored, sub_id),
                expires_at: gpg_key_expires_at(armored, sub_id),
                added_at: now,
                is_verified: false,
                can_sign: gpg_key_can_sign(armored, sub_id),
                can_encrypt_comms: gpg_key_can_encrypt(armored, sub_id),
                can_encrypt_storage: gpg_key_can_encrypt(armored, sub_id),
                can_certify: gpg_key_can_certify(armored, sub_id)
            )
        GpgKeyAdded(key: key, actor: owner)

    @guidance
        -- Web: POST /user/settings/keys (type=gpg). API: POST /api/v1/user/gpg_keys.
        -- An armored block holding several primary keys adds each of them
        -- (blocks repeating a primary key id are merged first: subkeys and
        -- identities are unioned); the whole upload fails if any primary key
        -- id is already registered. A subkey without its own lifetime inherits
        -- the primary key's expiry. The refusal when no identity matches tells
        -- the user the token to sign, since a signature lifts the email rule.
}

-- A user adds a GPG key together with a signature of their current token
-- made by that key (the same form / endpoint with the signature field set). The email rule is lifted and the key is stored verified.
-- Only the primary key that produced the signature is added.
-- from: models/asymkey/gpg_key_add.go:364
rule UserAddsGpgKeyProvenBySignature {
    when: UserAddsSignedGpgKey(owner, armored, challenge, signature)

    let key_id = gpg_token_signer_key_id(armored, signature)
    let identities = gpg_identity_emails(armored)

    requires: manages_own_gpg_keys(owner)
    requires: gpg_armored_key_parses(armored)
    requires: challenge.owner = owner
    requires: challenge.status = open
    requires: gpg_signs_token(armored, signature, challenge.token)
    requires: not exists GpgKey{key_id: key_id}

    ensures:
        let key = GpgKey.created(
            owner: owner,
            key_id: key_id,
            primary: null,
            public_key: gpg_primary_public_key(armored),
            identity_emails: identities,
            key_created_at: gpg_key_created_at(armored, key_id),
            expires_at: gpg_key_expires_at(armored, key_id),
            added_at: now,
            is_verified: true,
            can_sign: gpg_key_can_sign(armored, key_id),
            can_encrypt_comms: gpg_key_can_encrypt(armored, key_id),
            can_encrypt_storage: gpg_key_can_encrypt(armored, key_id),
            can_certify: gpg_key_can_certify(armored, key_id)
        )
        GpgKeyImport.created(key: key, armored: armored)
        for sub_id in gpg_subkey_ids(armored):
            GpgKey.created(
                owner: owner,
                key_id: sub_id,
                primary: key,
                public_key: gpg_subkey_public_key(armored, sub_id),
                identity_emails: {},
                key_created_at: gpg_key_created_at(armored, sub_id),
                expires_at: gpg_key_expires_at(armored, sub_id),
                added_at: now,
                is_verified: true,
                can_sign: gpg_key_can_sign(armored, sub_id),
                can_encrypt_comms: gpg_key_can_encrypt(armored, sub_id),
                can_encrypt_storage: gpg_key_can_encrypt(armored, sub_id),
                can_certify: gpg_key_can_certify(armored, sub_id)
            )
        GpgKeyAdded(key: key, actor: owner)
}

-- A user proves possession of an already registered primary key (or any of
-- its subkeys) by signing the token.
-- from: models/asymkey/gpg_key_verify.go:33
rule UserVerifiesGpgKey {
    when: UserVerifiesGpgKey(owner, key, challenge, signature)

    requires: key.owner = owner
    requires: key.is_primary
    requires: challenge.owner = owner
    requires: challenge.status = open
    requires: gpg_key_signs_token(key, signature, challenge.token)

    ensures: key.is_verified = true

    @guidance
        -- Web: POST /user/settings/keys (type=verify_gpg, key_id, signature).
        -- API: POST /api/v1/user/gpg_key_verify. Neither checks the
        -- manage_gpg_keys feature flag in Forgejo.
}

-- A user removes one of their primary GPG keys; its subkeys and the original
-- import go with it. Only the owner can remove a GPG key.
-- from: models/asymkey/gpg_key.go:230
rule UserDeletesGpgKey {
    when: UserDeletesGpgKey(owner, key)
    -- read before the record goes: an emission sees the resulting state
    let deleted_key_id = key.key_id

    requires: manages_own_gpg_keys(owner)
    requires: key.owner = owner
    requires: key.is_primary

    ensures:
        for sub in key.subkeys:
            not exists sub
    ensures:
        for imported in key.original_import:
            not exists imported
    ensures: not exists key
    ensures: GpgKeyDeleted(owner: owner, key_id: deleted_key_id, actor: owner)

    @guidance
        -- Web: POST /user/settings/keys/delete (type=gpg).
        -- API: DELETE /api/v1/user/gpg_keys/{id}.
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: signature verification
------------------------------------------------------------

-- An object without a signature is simply unverified.
-- from: models/asymkey/gpg_key_object_verification.go:105
rule VerifyUnsignedObject {
    when: SignatureVerificationRequested(repository, object_kind, object_id, committer_email, format?, signature?)

    requires: signature = null

    ensures: CommitVerification.created(
        repository: repository,
        object_kind: object_kind,
        object_id: object_id,
        committer_email: committer_email,
        committer: committer_account(committer_email),
        format: null,
        result: unverified,
        reason: not_signed,
        signer: null,
        signed_by_instance: false,
        signing_email: null,
        signing_gpg_key: null,
        signing_ssh_key: null,
        trust: null
    )
}

-- OpenPGP signatures. In order:
--   1. a registered key (primary or subkey) that may vouch for signatures
--      produced it: verified, credited to the key's owner;
--   2. the instance signing key (or the repository's default key) produced it:
--      verified, credited to the instance identity;
--   3. the signature names a key id we know (registered, or the instance
--      key) but that key did not produce it: warning (probable forgery);
--   4. otherwise: unverified, no matching key.
-- Committer and signer may differ; the trust model decides what that means.
-- from: models/asymkey/gpg_key_object_verification.go:80
rule VerifyOpenPgpSignature {
    when: SignatureVerificationRequested(repository, object_kind, object_id, committer_email, format?, signature?)

    let committer = committer_account(committer_email)
    let issuer_id = gpg_signature_issuer(signature)
    let signing_key = registered_gpg_key_that_signed(signature)

    requires: signature != null
    requires: format = openpgp

    ensures:
        if not gpg_signature_readable(signature):
            CommitVerification.created(
                repository: repository, object_kind: object_kind, object_id: object_id,
                committer_email: committer_email, committer: committer, format: openpgp,
                result: unverified, reason: unreadable_signature,
                signer: null, signed_by_instance: false, signing_email: null,
                signing_gpg_key: null, signing_ssh_key: null, trust: null
            )
        else if signing_key != null and signing_key.is_usable_for_signatures:
            let verification = CommitVerification.created(
                repository: repository, object_kind: object_kind, object_id: object_id,
                committer_email: committer_email, committer: committer, format: openpgp,
                result: verified, reason: signed_by_user_key,
                signer: signing_key.owner, signed_by_instance: false,
                signing_email: credited_email(signing_key, committer_email),
                signing_gpg_key: signing_key, signing_ssh_key: null, trust: null
            )
            SignatureVerified(verification: verification)
        else if instance_gpg_key_signed(repository, signature):
            let by_instance = CommitVerification.created(
                repository: repository, object_kind: object_kind, object_id: object_id,
                committer_email: committer_email, committer: committer, format: openpgp,
                result: verified, reason: signed_by_instance_key,
                signer: null, signed_by_instance: true,
                signing_email: instance_signing_email(repository),
                signing_gpg_key: null, signing_ssh_key: null, trust: null
            )
            SignatureVerified(verification: by_instance)
        else if exists GpgKey{key_id: issuer_id} or issuer_id = instance_gpg_key_id(repository):
            CommitVerification.created(
                repository: repository, object_kind: object_kind, object_id: object_id,
                committer_email: committer_email, committer: committer, format: openpgp,
                result: warning, reason: probable_bad_signature,
                signer: null, signed_by_instance: false, signing_email: null,
                signing_gpg_key: null, signing_ssh_key: null, trust: null
            )
        else:
            CommitVerification.created(
                repository: repository, object_kind: object_kind, object_id: object_id,
                committer_email: committer_email, committer: committer, format: openpgp,
                result: unverified, reason: no_matching_key,
                signer: null, signed_by_instance: false, signing_email: null,
                signing_gpg_key: null, signing_ssh_key: null, trust: null
            )

    @guidance
        -- registered_gpg_key_that_signed returns the primary key (resolving a
        -- subkey to its primary) whose signing-capable key validates the
        -- signature over the object's payload, looking first at the key id
        -- the signature names and then at the committer's own keys.
        -- The instance key is config.signing_key when signing_format is
        -- openpgp and it is an explicit key id; otherwise the key the server's
        -- git configuration signs with in this repository (SIGNING_KEY=default).
}

-- SSH signatures. Only verified personal keys of the committer count, and only
-- when the committer email is one of the committer's activated addresses (or
-- their no-reply address). Otherwise the instance SSH key is tried.
-- from: models/asymkey/ssh_key_object_verification.go:22
rule VerifySshSignature {
    when: SignatureVerificationRequested(repository, object_kind, object_id, committer_email, format?, signature?)

    let committer = committer_account(committer_email)
    let signing_key = registered_ssh_key_that_signed(signature)

    requires: signature != null
    requires: format = ssh

    ensures:
        if committer != null and signing_key != null
            and signing_key.kind = personal and signing_key.owner = committer and signing_key.is_verified:
            let verification = CommitVerification.created(
                repository: repository, object_kind: object_kind, object_id: object_id,
                committer_email: committer_email, committer: committer, format: ssh,
                result: verified, reason: signed_by_user_key,
                signer: committer, signed_by_instance: false, signing_email: committer_email,
                signing_gpg_key: null, signing_ssh_key: signing_key, trust: null
            )
            SignatureVerified(verification: verification)
        else if instance_ssh_key_signed(signature):
            let by_instance = CommitVerification.created(
                repository: repository, object_kind: object_kind, object_id: object_id,
                committer_email: committer_email, committer: committer, format: ssh,
                result: verified, reason: signed_by_instance_key,
                signer: null, signed_by_instance: true, signing_email: config.signing_email,
                signing_gpg_key: null, signing_ssh_key: null, trust: null
            )
            SignatureVerified(verification: by_instance)
        else:
            CommitVerification.created(
                repository: repository, object_kind: object_kind, object_id: object_id,
                committer_email: committer_email, committer: committer, format: ssh,
                result: unverified, reason: no_matching_key,
                signer: null, signed_by_instance: false, signing_email: null,
                signing_gpg_key: null, signing_ssh_key: null, trust: null
            )

    @guidance
        -- The SSH signature namespace for git objects is "git".
}

-- A verified signature is then judged by the repository's trust model.
--   committer model: trusted only when the signer is the committer (or, for
--     the instance key, when neither has an account and the emails agree);
--     otherwise unmatched.
--   collaborator model: the instance key is trusted; a user signer who is the
--     repository owner, a member of a team with code access to it, or a
--     collaborator is trusted; any other user signer is untrusted when they
--     are the committer and unmatched when they are not.
--   collaborator_committer model: as collaborator, but a trusted signer who is
--     not the committer becomes unmatched, and the instance key is untrusted
--     unless the committer has no account and the emails agree.
-- from: models/asymkey/gpg_key_object_verification.go:458
rule AssessSignatureTrust {
    when: SignatureVerified(verification)

    let repo_model = repository_trust_model(verification.repository)
    let model = if repo_model = instance_default: config.default_trust_model else: repo_model
    let signing_user = verification.signer
    let committing_user = verification.committer
    let same_person = signing_user != null and committing_user != null and signing_user = committing_user
    let instance_matches_committer = verification.signed_by_instance and committing_user = null
        and verification.signing_email = verification.committer_email
    let signer_is_member = signing_user != null and is_owner_member_or_collaborator(signing_user, verification.repository)

    requires: verification.result = verified

    ensures:
        if model = committer:
            if same_person or instance_matches_committer:
                verification.trust = trusted
            else:
                verification.trust = unmatched
        else if verification.signed_by_instance:
            if model = collaborator_committer and not instance_matches_committer:
                verification.trust = untrusted
            else:
                verification.trust = trusted
        else if not signer_is_member:
            if same_person:
                verification.trust = untrusted
            else:
                verification.trust = unmatched
        else if model = collaborator_committer and not same_person:
            verification.trust = unmatched
        else:
            verification.trust = trusted
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: instance signing of forge-made commits
------------------------------------------------------------

-- The initial commit of a repository created with auto-init (README, license,
-- .gitignore) or from a template.
-- from: services/asymkey/sign.go:139
rule DecideInitialCommitSigning {
    when: InitialCommitSigningRequested(actor, repository)

    let policy = SigningPolicy{operation: initial_commit}

    ensures:
        if not instance_signing_key_available(repository):
            SigningDecision.created(operation: initial_commit, actor: actor, repository: repository,
                will_sign: false, refusal: no_instance_key, signer_name: null, signer_email: null)
        else if policy.mode = never:
            SigningDecision.created(operation: initial_commit, actor: actor, repository: repository,
                will_sign: false, refusal: policy_never, signer_name: null, signer_email: null)
        else if policy.mode = conditional and policy.requires_registered_key and not has_registered_key(actor):
            SigningDecision.created(operation: initial_commit, actor: actor, repository: repository,
                will_sign: false, refusal: no_registered_key, signer_name: null, signer_email: null)
        else if policy.mode = conditional and policy.requires_two_factor and not has_two_factor(actor):
            SigningDecision.created(operation: initial_commit, actor: actor, repository: repository,
                will_sign: false, refusal: no_two_factor, signer_name: null, signer_email: null)
        else:
            SigningDecision.created(operation: initial_commit, actor: actor, repository: repository,
                will_sign: true, refusal: null,
                signer_name: instance_signing_name(repository), signer_email: instance_signing_email(repository))
}

-- Commits made through the web editor and file APIs (create / update / delete
-- files, apply patch, cherry-pick, revert).
-- from: services/asymkey/sign.go:229
rule DecideWebEditSigning {
    when: WebEditSigningRequested(actor, repository, parent_verified)

    let policy = SigningPolicy{operation: web_edit}

    ensures:
        if not instance_signing_key_available(repository):
            SigningDecision.created(operation: web_edit, actor: actor, repository: repository,
                will_sign: false, refusal: no_instance_key, signer_name: null, signer_email: null)
        else if policy.mode = never:
            SigningDecision.created(operation: web_edit, actor: actor, repository: repository,
                will_sign: false, refusal: policy_never, signer_name: null, signer_email: null)
        else if policy.mode = conditional and policy.requires_registered_key and not has_registered_key(actor):
            SigningDecision.created(operation: web_edit, actor: actor, repository: repository,
                will_sign: false, refusal: no_registered_key, signer_name: null, signer_email: null)
        else if policy.mode = conditional and policy.requires_two_factor and not has_two_factor(actor):
            SigningDecision.created(operation: web_edit, actor: actor, repository: repository,
                will_sign: false, refusal: no_two_factor, signer_name: null, signer_email: null)
        else if policy.mode = conditional and policy.requires_parent_signed and not parent_verified:
            SigningDecision.created(operation: web_edit, actor: actor, repository: repository,
                will_sign: false, refusal: parent_unsigned, signer_name: null, signer_email: null)
        else:
            SigningDecision.created(operation: web_edit, actor: actor, repository: repository,
                will_sign: true, refusal: null,
                signer_name: instance_signing_name(repository), signer_email: instance_signing_email(repository))

    @guidance
        -- `parent_verified` is the CommitVerification result of the commit
        -- the edit is made on top of (verified = true).
}

-- Commits to a repository's wiki.
-- from: services/asymkey/sign.go:175
rule DecideWikiSigning {
    when: WikiEditSigningRequested(actor, repository, wiki_head_verified)

    let policy = SigningPolicy{operation: wiki_edit}

    ensures:
        if not instance_signing_key_available(repository):
            SigningDecision.created(operation: wiki_edit, actor: actor, repository: repository,
                will_sign: false, refusal: no_instance_key, signer_name: null, signer_email: null)
        else if policy.mode = never:
            SigningDecision.created(operation: wiki_edit, actor: actor, repository: repository,
                will_sign: false, refusal: policy_never, signer_name: null, signer_email: null)
        else if policy.mode = conditional and policy.requires_registered_key and not has_registered_key(actor):
            SigningDecision.created(operation: wiki_edit, actor: actor, repository: repository,
                will_sign: false, refusal: no_registered_key, signer_name: null, signer_email: null)
        else if policy.mode = conditional and policy.requires_two_factor and not has_two_factor(actor):
            SigningDecision.created(operation: wiki_edit, actor: actor, repository: repository,
                will_sign: false, refusal: no_two_factor, signer_name: null, signer_email: null)
        else if policy.mode = conditional and policy.requires_parent_signed and not wiki_head_verified:
            SigningDecision.created(operation: wiki_edit, actor: actor, repository: repository,
                will_sign: false, refusal: parent_unsigned, signer_name: null, signer_email: null)
        else:
            SigningDecision.created(operation: wiki_edit, actor: actor, repository: repository,
                will_sign: true, refusal: null,
                signer_name: instance_signing_name(repository), signer_email: instance_signing_email(repository))
}

-- The merge commit (or rebased / squashed commits) created when a pull
-- request is merged through the forge.
-- from: services/asymkey/sign.go:282
rule DecideMergeSigning {
    when: MergeSigningRequested(actor, pull, base_verified, head_verified, all_commits_verified, has_approval)

    let repository = pull.base_repository
    let policy = SigningPolicy{operation: merge}

    ensures:
        if not instance_signing_key_available(repository):
            SigningDecision.created(operation: merge, actor: actor, repository: repository,
                will_sign: false, refusal: no_instance_key, signer_name: null, signer_email: null)
        else if policy.mode = never:
            SigningDecision.created(operation: merge, actor: actor, repository: repository,
                will_sign: false, refusal: policy_never, signer_name: null, signer_email: null)
        else if policy.mode = conditional and policy.requires_registered_key and not has_registered_key(actor):
            SigningDecision.created(operation: merge, actor: actor, repository: repository,
                will_sign: false, refusal: no_registered_key, signer_name: null, signer_email: null)
        else if policy.mode = conditional and policy.requires_two_factor and not has_two_factor(actor):
            SigningDecision.created(operation: merge, actor: actor, repository: repository,
                will_sign: false, refusal: no_two_factor, signer_name: null, signer_email: null)
        else if policy.mode = conditional and policy.requires_approval and not has_approval:
            SigningDecision.created(operation: merge, actor: actor, repository: repository,
                will_sign: false, refusal: not_approved, signer_name: null, signer_email: null)
        else if policy.mode = conditional and policy.requires_base_signed and not base_verified:
            SigningDecision.created(operation: merge, actor: actor, repository: repository,
                will_sign: false, refusal: base_unsigned, signer_name: null, signer_email: null)
        else if policy.mode = conditional and policy.requires_head_signed and not head_verified:
            SigningDecision.created(operation: merge, actor: actor, repository: repository,
                will_sign: false, refusal: head_unsigned, signer_name: null, signer_email: null)
        else if policy.mode = conditional and policy.requires_commits_signed and not all_commits_verified:
            SigningDecision.created(operation: merge, actor: actor, repository: repository,
                will_sign: false, refusal: commits_unsigned, signer_name: null, signer_email: null)
        else:
            SigningDecision.created(operation: merge, actor: actor, repository: repository,
                will_sign: true, refusal: null,
                signer_name: instance_signing_name(repository), signer_email: instance_signing_email(repository))

    @guidance
        -- `has_approval`: the base branch has a protection rule and the pull
        -- request has at least one approval that counts under it.
        -- `all_commits_verified`: the head commit and every commit between the
        -- merge base and the head are verified.
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: SSH authentication key lookup
------------------------------------------------------------

-- A git client offers a plain public key. It is accepted when it is a
-- registered personal or deploy key; what it may do is decided by code/access.
-- from: modules/ssh/ssh.go:266
rule AuthenticateSshPublicKey {
    when: SshClientPresentsPublicKey(connection, presented_key)

    let key = SshKey{fingerprint: ssh_fingerprint(presented_key)}

    requires: not config.ssh_disabled
    requires: exists key
    requires: key.kind in {personal, deploy}

    ensures: SshKeyAuthenticated(connection: connection, key: key)

    @guidance
        -- Built-in server: the public-key callback. External OpenSSH: the
        -- AuthorizedKeysCommand / authorized_keys line, which carries the key
        -- id ("serv key-<id>"); routers/private/key.go answers fingerprint
        -- lookups for AuthorizedKeysCommand.
}

-- A git client offers a user certificate. It is accepted when it was signed
-- by a trusted CA and is valid for a principal some user has registered;
-- the client then authenticates as that principal's owner.
-- from: modules/ssh/ssh.go:186
rule AuthenticateSshCertificate {
    when: SshClientPresentsCertificate(connection, certificate)

    let key = registered_principal_for(certificate)

    requires: not config.ssh_disabled
    requires: config.trusted_user_ca_keys_configured
    requires: is_user_certificate(certificate)
    requires: key != null
    requires: certificate_signed_by_trusted_ca(certificate)
    requires: certificate_valid_for(certificate, key.content)

    ensures: SshKeyAuthenticated(connection: connection, key: key)

    @guidance
        -- Principals are tried in the order the certificate lists them; a
        -- principal whose certificate check fails (expired, wrong principal,
        -- critical options) stops the whole attempt rather than falling
        -- through to the next.
}

-- After a successful git operation over SSH, the key (and, for a deploy key,
-- its grant on that repository) is marked as used.
-- from: routers/private/key.go:17
rule RecordSshKeyUse {
    when: SshKeyUsedForRepository(key, repository)

    let grant = DeployKey{repository: repository, key: key}

    ensures: key.last_used_at = now
    ensures:
        if exists grant:
            grant.last_used_at = now
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Invariants
------------------------------------------------------------

-- No two registered SSH keys (of any kind) share a fingerprint.
invariant UniqueSshFingerprint {
    for a in SshKeys:
        for b in SshKeys:
            a != b and a.fingerprint != null implies a.fingerprint != b.fingerprint
}

-- Titles are unique per owner (principals use the principal as title).
invariant UniqueKeyTitlePerOwner {
    for a in SshKeys:
        for b in SshKeys:
            a != b and a.owner != null and a.owner = b.owner implies a.name != b.name
}

-- A principal belongs to at most one user.
invariant UniquePrincipal {
    for a in SshKeys:
        for b in SshKeys:
            a != b and a.kind = principal and b.kind = principal implies a.content != b.content
}

-- Deploy key material has no owner; personal keys and principals always do.
invariant DeployKeysAreOwnerless {
    for k in SshKeys:
        (k.kind = deploy implies k.owner = null) and (k.kind != deploy implies k.owner != null)
}

-- Only principals lack a fingerprint.
invariant PrincipalsHaveNoFingerprint {
    for k in SshKeys:
        (k.kind = principal) = (k.fingerprint = null)
}

-- Repository grants only ever point at deploy key material.
invariant GrantsUseDeployMaterial {
    for d in DeployKeys:
        d.key.kind = deploy
}

-- One grant per (repository, key) and per (repository, title).
invariant UniqueDeployKeyPerRepository {
    for a in DeployKeys:
        for b in DeployKeys:
            a != b and a.repository = b.repository implies (a.key != b.key and a.name != b.name)
}

-- Deploy key material exists only while some repository uses it.
invariant DeployMaterialIsAttached {
    for k in SshKeys:
        k.kind = deploy implies k.attachments.count > 0
}

-- GPG key ids are unique across the instance (primary keys and subkeys).
invariant UniqueGpgKeyId {
    for a in GpgKeys:
        for b in GpgKeys:
            a != b implies a.key_id != b.key_id
}

-- Subkeys hang directly off a primary key of the same owner.
invariant SubkeysBelongToPrimaryOwner {
    for k in GpgKeys:
        k.primary != null implies (k.primary.owner = k.owner and k.primary.primary = null)
}

-- Only primary keys carry identities and an original import.
invariant ImportsAreForPrimaryKeys {
    for i in GpgKeyImports:
        i.key.primary = null
}

-- A verified result names who (or what) signed; others name nobody.
invariant VerifiedResultsNameASigner {
    for v in CommitVerifications:
        (v.result = verified implies (v.signer != null or v.signed_by_instance))
        and (v.result != verified implies (v.signer = null and not v.signed_by_instance and v.trust = null))
}

-- Exactly one signing policy per operation.
invariant OneSigningPolicyPerOperation {
    for a in SigningPolicys:
        for b in SigningPolicys:
            a != b implies a.operation != b.operation
}

-- Conditions only exist where they make sense.
invariant SigningConditionsApply {
    for p in SigningPolicys:
        (p.operation = initial_commit implies not p.requires_parent_signed)
        and (p.operation != merge implies
            not (p.requires_base_signed or p.requires_head_signed or p.requires_commits_signed or p.requires_approval))
        and (p.operation = merge implies not p.requires_parent_signed)
}

-- A refusal is recorded exactly when the forge declines to sign.
invariant RefusalExplainsDecision {
    for d in SigningDecisions:
        (d.will_sign = false) = (d.refusal != null)
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Actor Declarations
------------------------------------------------------------

-- An administrator of one repository (owner, org owner, team or collaborator
-- with admin access, or site admin) is access/RepoAdmin.

-- An administrator of the repository a deploy key is attached to.
actor DeployKeyAdministrator {
    within: DeployKey
    identified_by: accounts/User where is_repo_admin(this, within.repository)
}

-- The forge's own subsystems calling into this module.
actor InternalCaller {
    identified_by: ForgeSubsystem where name != ""
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Surfaces
------------------------------------------------------------

-- The signed-in user's key settings page: adding keys and asking for a token.
surface KeySettings {
    facing owner: access/SignedInUser

    exposes:
        config.ssh_disabled
        config.principals_allow_anything
        config.principals_allow_username
        config.principals_allow_email
        manages_own_ssh_keys(owner)
        manages_own_gpg_keys(owner)

    provides:
        UserAddsSshKey(owner, title, content)
            when manages_own_ssh_keys(owner)
        UserAddsGpgKey(owner, armored)
            when manages_own_gpg_keys(owner)
        UserAddsSignedGpgKey(owner, armored, challenge, signature)
            when manages_own_gpg_keys(owner)
        UserAddsPrincipal(owner, principal)
            when not config.ssh_disabled
        UserRequestsVerificationToken(owner)

    @guidance
        -- Web: GET/POST /user/settings/keys (form field `type` = ssh | gpg |
        -- principal | verify_ssh | verify_gpg), POST /user/settings/keys/delete.
        -- API: GET/POST /api/v1/user/keys, GET/DELETE /api/v1/user/keys/{id},
        -- GET/POST /api/v1/user/gpg_keys, GET/DELETE /api/v1/user/gpg_keys/{id},
        -- GET /api/v1/user/gpg_key_token, POST /api/v1/user/gpg_key_verify.
        -- API access needs a token with the user scope.
}

-- The token a user is asked to sign.
surface VerificationTokenView {
    facing owner: access/SignedInUser
    context challenge: VerificationChallenge where owner = owner and status = open

    exposes:
        challenge.token
        challenge.expires_at

    timeout:
        VerificationChallengeExpires
}

-- One of the user's own personal SSH keys.
surface OwnSshKey {
    facing owner: access/SignedInUser
    context key: SshKey where owner = owner and kind = personal

    exposes:
        key.name
        key.content
        key.fingerprint
        key.algorithm
        key.bits
        key.is_verified
        key.created_at
        key.last_used_at
        key.has_recent_activity
        key.is_externally_managed

    provides:
        UserVerifiesSshKey(owner, key, challenge, signature)
            when not key.is_verified and manages_own_ssh_keys(owner)
        UserDeletesSshKey(owner, key)
            when not key.is_externally_managed and manages_own_ssh_keys(owner)

    @guarantee ExternallyManagedKeysAreReadOnly
        -- A key supplied by an LDAP or OAuth2 source is shown, marked as
        -- managed elsewhere, and cannot be removed by its owner.
}

-- One of the user's own SSH certificate principals.
surface OwnPrincipal {
    facing owner: access/SignedInUser
    context key: SshKey where owner = owner and kind = principal

    exposes:
        key.content
        key.created_at
        key.last_used_at

    provides:
        UserDeletesPrincipal(owner, key)
}

-- One of the user's own primary GPG keys.
surface OwnGpgKey {
    facing owner: access/SignedInUser
    context key: GpgKey where owner = owner and primary = null

    exposes:
        key.key_id
        key.identity_emails
        key.matched_emails
        key.is_verified
        key.can_sign
        key.can_encrypt_comms
        key.can_encrypt_storage
        key.can_certify
        key.key_created_at
        key.expires_at
        key.added_at
        for sub in key.subkeys:
            sub.key_id
            sub.can_sign
            sub.expires_at

    provides:
        UserVerifiesGpgKey(owner, key, challenge, signature)
            when not key.is_verified
        UserDeletesGpgKey(owner, key)
            when manages_own_gpg_keys(owner)
}

-- The deploy keys page of a repository.
surface RepositoryDeployKeys {
    facing admin: access/RepoAdmin
    context repository: repositories/Repository

    exposes:
        config.ssh_disabled

    provides:
        RepoAdminAddsDeployKey(admin, repository, title, content, access)

    @guidance
        -- Web: GET/POST /{owner}/{repo}/settings/keys,
        -- POST /{owner}/{repo}/settings/keys/delete.
        -- API: GET/POST /api/v1/repos/{owner}/{repo}/keys (filters: key_id,
        -- fingerprint), GET/DELETE /api/v1/repos/{owner}/{repo}/keys/{id}.
}

-- One deploy key of a repository, as its administrators see it.
surface RepositoryDeployKey {
    facing admin: DeployKeyAdministrator
    context deploy_key: DeployKey

    exposes:
        deploy_key.name
        deploy_key.access
        deploy_key.created_at
        deploy_key.last_used_at
        deploy_key.has_recent_activity
        deploy_key.key.fingerprint
        deploy_key.key.content

    provides:
        RepoAdminDeletesDeployKey(admin, deploy_key)
}

-- A user's public SSH keys, as anyone who may see the user's profile sees
-- them. Principals and deploy keys are never listed.
surface PublicSshKeys {
    facing viewer: accounts/User
    context key: SshKey where kind = personal and owner.visible_to(viewer)

    exposes:
        key.public_line
        key.name
        key.fingerprint
        key.is_verified
        key.created_at
        key.last_used_at

    @guidance
        -- Web: GET /{username}.keys (one public_line per key, comments
        -- stripped, a "# Note" line when there are none).
        -- API: GET /api/v1/users/{username}/keys; the owner and site admins
        -- also see key_type, read_only and the owner object.
        -- Anonymous visitors see what a public profile shows.
}

-- A user's public GPG keys.
surface PublicGpgKeys {
    facing viewer: accounts/User
    context key: GpgKey where primary = null and owner.visible_to(viewer)

    exposes:
        key.key_id
        key.public_key
        key.identity_emails
        key.is_verified
        key.expires_at
        for imported in key.original_import:
            imported.armored

    @guidance
        -- Web: GET /{username}.gpg returns one armored block re-exporting
        -- every primary key from its original import; keys with no import
        -- are listed in a "Note" header asking for a re-upload.
        -- API: GET /api/v1/users/{username}/gpg_keys.
}

-- The forge's own public signing keys.
surface InstanceSigningKeys {
    facing viewer: accounts/User
    context repository: repositories/Repository

    exposes:
        instance_gpg_public_key(repository)
        instance_ssh_public_key()

    @guidance
        -- API: GET /api/v1/signing-key.gpg, GET /api/v1/signing-key.ssh,
        -- GET /api/v1/repos/{owner}/{repo}/signing-key.gpg (the key used in
        -- that repository, which may differ under SIGNING_KEY=default).
        -- Empty / not found when no key is configured.
}

-- The verification badge on a commit or tag.
surface SignatureBadge {
    facing viewer: accounts/User
    context verification: CommitVerification where can_read_code(viewer, repository)

    exposes:
        verification.result
        verification.reason
        verification.trust
        verification.signer
        verification.signed_by_instance
        verification.signing_email
        verification.signing_gpg_key
        verification.signing_ssh_key

    @guidance
        -- Shown on commit lists, the commit page, tags/releases, pull request
        -- commit lists and the commit graph; included as `verification` in the
        -- API commit object and in push webhook payloads.
        -- Colour: verified+trusted green, verified+untrusted yellow,
        -- verified+unmatched orange, warning red, unverified grey.
}

-- The SSH transport asking which key a client holds.
surface SshKeyResolution {
    facing _: InternalCaller

    provides:
        SshClientPresentsPublicKey(connection, presented_key)
        SshClientPresentsCertificate(connection, certificate)
        SshKeyUsedForRepository(key, repository)

    @guidance
        -- Internal routes: GET /api/internal/serv/none/{keyid},
        -- GET /api/internal/serv/command/{keyid}/{owner}/{repo},
        -- POST /api/internal/ssh/{id}/update/{repoid},
        -- POST /api/internal/ssh/authorized_keys (fingerprint lookup).
}

-- Other modules asking for verification and signing decisions.
surface SigningService {
    facing _: InternalCaller

    provides:
        SignatureVerificationRequested(repository, object_kind, object_id, committer_email, format?, signature?)
        InitialCommitSigningRequested(actor, repository)
        WebEditSigningRequested(actor, repository, parent_verified)
        WikiEditSigningRequested(actor, repository, wiki_head_verified)
        MergeSigningRequested(actor, pull, base_verified, head_verified, all_commits_verified, has_approval)
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Open Questions
------------------------------------------------------------

open question "Adding personal SSH keys and deploy keys is allowed while DISABLE_SSH is set (only principals check it). Should a rebuild refuse key registration when SSH is disabled, or keep keys for commit signature verification?"
open question "Externally supplied SSH keys (LDAP / OAuth2) bypass the algorithm and minimum-size policy. Should the policy apply to them too?"
open question "Commit trust for SSH-signed commits: Forgejo only consults the collaborator check for GPG signing keys, so an SSH signature by a non-collaborator is 'trusted' under the collaborator models. The spec applies the same rule to both formats; confirm."
open question "Signatures by expired or revoked GPG keys still verify (expiry is only displayed). Should verification take key expiry into account?"
open question "GET /api/v1/user/keys/{id} returns any user's key by id and GET /api/v1/user/keys?fingerprint=... searches keys of all users including deploy keys. Is cross-user lookup intended (it is how 'who owns this key' works) or should it be limited to the caller's keys?"
open question "The GPG verify endpoints ignore the manage_gpg_keys feature flag, while adding and deleting honour it. Intended?"
open question "Deploy keys can be added to archived repositories and mirrors. Should that be refused like other settings changes on archived repositories?"
open question "The signing policy lists are order-sensitive in Forgejo (the first of never/always wins); the spec says never wins over always. Confirm."
open question "When several principals of one certificate are registered, Forgejo stops at the first one whose certificate check fails instead of trying the rest. Keep or fall through?"

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Requests to other modules
------------------------------------------------------------

-- REQUEST authentication/AuthSource.provides_ssh_keys: true for LDAP sources with an SSH public key attribute and OAuth2 sources configured to provide SSH keys; drives is_externally_managed and key sync.
-- REQUEST authentication/AuthSource.name: used to name synchronised keys "<source>-<fingerprint>".
-- REQUEST authentication: provide has_two_factor(user) (TOTP or WebAuthn enrolled) — used locally as black box has_two_factor.
-- REQUEST repositories/Repository.trust_model: keys/TrustModel, settable by repo admins (web settings, API create/edit `trust_model`) — used locally as black box repository_trust_model.
-- REQUEST repositories: emit RepositoryDeleted(repository) so deploy keys are detached.
-- REQUEST repositories / access: provide is_owner_member_or_collaborator(user, repository): owner, member of a team with code access to the repository, or collaborator.
-- REQUEST accounts: manages_own_ssh_keys(user) / manages_own_gpg_keys(user) = not user.feature_disabled(manage_ssh_keys / manage_gpg_keys); used locally as black boxes because parameterised derived values are not evaluated by the journey walker.
-- REQUEST access: is_repo_admin(user, repository) and can_read_code(user, repository) (access/is_repo_admin, access/can_read(user, repository, code)); used locally as black boxes because qualified black boxes are not evaluated by the journey walker.
-- REQUEST accounts: committer_account(email) — the user owning an activated address (or the user's no-reply address) equal to email, case-insensitive.
-- REQUEST code: raise SignatureVerificationRequested for commits/tags shown or checked (protected-branch "require signed commits"), raise SshClientPresents* / SshKeyUsedForRepository from the SSH transport, and react to SshKeyAuthenticated(connection, key) to decide repository access (deploy key access read_only < write request => refuse).
-- REQUEST code / repositories / wiki / pulls: ask WebEditSigningRequested / InitialCommitSigningRequested / WikiEditSigningRequested / MergeSigningRequested before creating commits and sign when SigningDecision.will_sign.
-- REQUEST pulls/PullRequest.base_repository: used to find the repository a merge is signed in.
